 2467 Q 1414 2611 1619 2694 Q 1824 2778 2093 2778 Q 2477 2778 2774 2611 Q 3072 2445 3241 2134 Q 3411 1824 3411 1402 Q 3411 966 3225 630 Q 3040 294 2707 108 Q 2374 -77 1926 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2214 390 2422 499 Q 2630 608 2742 819 Q 2854 1030 2854 1331 L 2854 1382 Q 2854 1683 2742 1894 Q 2630 2106 2422 2214 Q 2214 2323 1920 2323 Q 1626 2323 1418 2214 Q 1210 2106 1098 1894 Q 986 1683 986 1382 L 986 1331 Q 986 1030 1098 819 Q 1210 608 1418 499 Q 1626 390 1920 390 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-7b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(142.049148 91.432) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" d=\"M 1920 -77 Q 1414 -77 1068 92 Q 723 262 547 556 Q 371 851 371 1216 Q 371 1670 620 1942 Q 870 2214 1274 2323 L 1274 2374 Q 922 2496 714 2768 Q 506 3040 506 3424 Q 506 3936 880 4240 Q 1254 4544 1920 4544 Q 2586 4544 2960 4240 Q 3334 3936 3334 3424 Q 3334 3040 3126 2768 Q 2918 2496 2566 2374 L 2566 2323 Q 2970 2214 3219 1942 Q 3469 1670 3469 1216 Q 3469 851 3293 556 Q 3117 262 2774 92 Q 2432 -77 1920 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2387 390 2643 601 Q 2899 813 2899 1190 L 2899 1325 Q 2899 1702 2643 1913 Q 2387 2125 1920 2125 Q 1453 2125 1197 1913 Q 941 1702 941 1325 L 941 1190 Q 941 813 1197 601 Q 1453 390 1920 390 z\nM 1920 2573 Q 2336 2573 2557 2755 Q 2778 2938 2778 3277 L 2778 3373 Q 2778 3712 2557 3894 Q 2336 4077 1920 4077 Q 1504 4077 1283 3894 Q 1062 3712 1062 3373 L 1062 3277 Q 1062 2938 1283 2755 Q 1504 2573 1920 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-7b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(205.171875 72.424) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-7b\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(270.694602 47.08) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-7b\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(336.21733 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-7b\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pa48246664e\"><rect x=\"40.7\" y=\"11.264\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"133.056\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Share of pupils whose families pay for maths tutoring, by household income (%)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Average share paying for maths tutoring = average of the five income groups = (6% + 8% + 11% + 15% + 20%) ÷ 5 = <b>12%</b> (each group is one fifth of pupils).</p> <p>Tutored pupils: 3.6M × 12% = <b>432k</b>.</p> <p>Spend: 432k × 30 sessions × $35 = <b>$454M a year</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> a market of roughly $450M, heavily skewed to higher-income families, who are the most likely to buy one-to-one tutors.</p>","note":"Pupils in years 7 to 11 in England: about 3.6M. Tutored pupils have about 30 sessions a year at around $35. All figures are case assumptions."},{"q":"How many students does BrightStep need to reach $10M, and what share of tutored pupils is that?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Revenue per student: 30 lessons × $12 = $360 a year.</p> <p>Students needed: $10M ÷ $360 ≈ <b>27.8k</b>, which is <b>6.4%</b> of today's 432k tutored pupils.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> ambitious but plausible, and BrightStep's low price could also attract families who don't pay for tutoring today, especially in the lower-income groups where only 6% to 8% currently pay.</p>"},{"q":"What would make you more or less confident in the $10M target?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>More confident:</b> schools buying lessons for whole groups (one sale, many pupils); strong retention from autumn to exam season; a low cost to win each family</li> <li><b>Less confident:</b> most tutoring is bought just before exams (fewer than 30 sessions); one-to-one tutors cutting prices online; families seeing small groups as \"not real tutoring\"</li> <li><b>Test:</b> retention from September to May and the cost of winning each paying family</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Paid maths tutoring for secondary pupils in England is worth roughly $454M a year: about 432k pupils, 30 sessions each at around $35. BrightStep's $10M target needs about 27.8k students, 6.4% of today's tutored pupils, which is achievable if its $12 price brings in families who can't afford one-to-one tutors. I'd back the plan subject to two checks: retention through the school year, and the cost of acquiring each family. Next step: run a term-long pilot with two schools to measure both.","great":["Uses the income split to get the average, not a guess","Keeps units clear: pupils, sessions, price","Compares the target with the size of the market","Sees the low price could expand the market"],"id":27,"slug":"brightstep-tutoring"}